ort olympiad; import geometry; import graph; size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));\npair[] vertices;\nfor(int i = 0; i < 6; ++i){\n\nvertices[i] = dir(30 + 60*i);\n}\ndraw(vertices[0]--vertices[2]--vertices[4]--cycle);\ndraw(vertices[1]--vertices[3]--vertices[5]--cycle);\nlabel(\"$D$\",vertices[0],NE); label(\"$C$\",vertices[1],N); label(\"$B$\",vertices[2],NW); label(\"$A$\",vertices[3],SW);\nlabel(\"$F$\",vertices[4],S); label(\"$E$\",vertices[5],SE);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"fb98ec97ffbc1747ab50d81f4454b2a4067298d8aa503ecf44a5971975db53f0"},"seconds":36.59651494026184,"seed":681125408605337258,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the area of the entire star, we can break it down into the areas of the central hexagon and the six equilateral triangles that surround it. Given that $\\overline{AC}$ is 3 units long, and knowing that $AC$ spans two sides of the equilateral triangles, we can deduce that each side of the triangles and the hexagon is $3/2 = 1.5$ units long.\n\n1. **Calculate the area of one equilateral triangle:**\n   The formula for the area of an equilateral triangle with side length $s$ is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} s^2\n   \\]\n   For our triangles, the side length $s = 1.5$ units, so the area of one triangle is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times (1.5)^2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times \\frac{9}{4} = \\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{16}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the area of the central hexagon:**\n   The central hexagon can be divided into 6 equilateral triangles, each with side length $1.5$ units. Therefore, the area of the hexagon is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of hexagon} = 6 \\times \\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{16} = \\frac{54\\sqrt{3}}{16} = \\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{8}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total area of the six surrounding triangles:**\n   There are 6 surrounding triangles, each with the same area as the triangles we calculated earlier:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total area of six triangles} = 6 \\times \\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{16} = \\frac{54\\sqrt{3}}{16} = \\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{8}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total area of the star:**\n   The total area of the star is the sum of the area of the central hexagon and the area of the six surrounding triangles:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total area} = \\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{8} + \\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{8} = \\frac{54\\sqrt{3}}{8} = \\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{4}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the area of the entire star is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{4}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{4}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
